+
+## Diagnostics connections
+
+The homepage includes independent browser-side connection checks for a private
+LAN test device and a loopback companion CLI. Edit the example URLs to match
+your services (`http://192.168.1.100:8080/api/status` and
+`http://127.0.0.1:45678/health`); these are illustrative endpoints, not bundled
+services. Each Connect click sends one GET request and displays the HTTP status,
+elapsed time, and JSON or text response. There is no discovery, polling, server
+proxy, or persistent connection.
+
+Serve the site over HTTPS (localhost is also a secure context for development).
+Use a browser supporting Local Network Access. The two targets use separate
+`local-network` and `loopback-network` permission checks and explicit fetch
+`targetAddressSpace` values. Unsupported permission queries are caught; the
+user can still attempt a connection, subject to their browser's restrictions.
+Denied permissions must be restored in the browser's site settings. Requests
+time out after 15 seconds and can be canceled.
+
+The device must be reachable from the reader's LAN, and the CLI must expose an
+HTTP service on the reader's machine. Both endpoints must support standard CORS,
+for example `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://your-deployed-site.example`
+(the origin has no path, including no `/devtools-times/`). Requests omit
+credentials and referrers and reject redirects. Responses are rendered as text
+and the displayed output is capped at 8,000 characters. Browser network errors
+cannot reliably distinguish permission denial, CORS, TLS, and an offline service;
+the widget provides troubleshooting guidance rather than claiming a cause.
+
+The widget runs in the top-level page, where both network permissions default to
+`self`. A deployment must not disable them with a restrictive Permissions-Policy
+header. No access is delegated to third-party frames. See the
+[Chrome Local Network Access guide](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/security/local-network-access)
+for browser permission and deployment details.
